  "difficulty": 1,
  "marks": 1,
  "estimatedSeconds": 90,
  "stem": "Which is the formula for integration by parts?",
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "content": "$\\displaystyle\\int u\\frac{dv}{dx}\\,dx = uv - \\int v\\frac{du}{dx}\\,dx$",
    "correct": true,
    "rationale": "Correct: the product rule integrated and rearranged (MF19)."
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "content": "$\\displaystyle\\int u\\frac{dv}{dx}\\,dx = uv + \\int v\\frac{du}{dx}\\,dx$",
    "rationale": "The second term is subtracted, not added."
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "content": "$\\displaystyle\\int u\\frac{dv}{dx}\\,dx = \\frac{du}{dx}\\frac{dv}{dx}$",
    "rationale": "This multiplies two derivatives and is not an integral rule."
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "content": "$\\displaystyle\\int u\\frac{dv}{dx}\\,dx = u\\int v\\,dx - v\\int u\\,dx$",
    "rationale": "This mixes up the roles of u and v; there is no such rule."
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "From $\\frac{d}{dx}(uv) = u\\frac{dv}{dx} + v\\frac{du}{dx}$, integrate and rearrange: $\\int u\\frac{dv}{dx}\\,dx = uv - \\int v\\frac{du}{dx}\\,dx$.",
